## Generated API client

`Packages/Contracts` is generated from `contracts/openapi.yaml` with OpenAPI
Generator (Swift 5, async/await). `Core` re-exports the generated models as
`User`, `AuthSession`, `Product` and friends, and its `APIClient` calls the
generated `AuthAPI`, `ProductsAPI` and `AgentAPI`. The SSE stream stays a small
custom transport because OpenAPI does not model server-sent events.

Do not edit `Packages/Contracts` by hand. After changing a contract fragment:

```sh
./scripts/generate-contracts.sh          # from apps/ios
```

`scripts/generate-contracts.sh --check` verifies the recorded contract hash;
`--verify` regenerates in a temporary directory and diffs the result. Both
need Node and Java 17+. Generation is also wired to `make contracts` and
`make contracts-verify-native` at the project root.

## UI seam

`Packages/Core/Sources/Core/AppComponents.swift` defines the visual slots
(`productRow`, `emptyState`, `primaryButton`, `chatMessage`, `composer`,
`toolCall`) and the `\.appComponents` SwiftUI environment value. `App.swift`
injects `AppComponents.reference`; a project replaces a closure (or the whole
value) there without editing feature data flow. The product list already reads
its row and empty state, and the create action, through this seam.

## Assistant

The first destination is the Assistant tab. It posts to
`/api/v1/agent/runs`, consumes the SSE run stream through
`APIClient.streamAgentRun`, and renders text and tool calls through
`AppComponents`. When the coordinator selects the products agent, the screen
offers an "Open products" action; direct product/profile destinations remain.
The screen never classifies intent or calls a model provider.

## Configuration

`API_BASE_URL` in `App/Info.plist` is the API root. The checked-in value is the
documented local development default:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
```

Point it at the project's API for each environment. The API client reads the
key at launch and falls back to the same local default when the key is absent.
`NSAllowsLocalNetworking` keeps plain HTTP working for that local default;
production builds should use HTTPS and may remove the exception.

{% if enabled('ui.mobile.auth') %}
Authentication stores the session token in the Keychain (accessible after first
unlock, this device only). Every authenticated request sends
`Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A 401 clears the token and returns the app to
sign-in.
{% endif %}

## Behaviour

- Compact width uses a `TabView` with a `NavigationStack` per tab.
{% if enabled('ui.mobile.responsive') %}
- Regular width (iPad) uses a `NavigationSplitView` with a sidebar.
{% if enabled('ui.mobile.auth') %}
  The auth screen becomes a centered card with a maximum width.
{% endif %}
{% if enabled('ui.mobile.crud') %}
  Products uses a list/detail split view.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
- Semantic fonts and colours follow Dynamic Type, dark mode and safe areas;
  forms scroll so the keyboard never covers the active field.
{% if enabled('ui.mobile.crud') %}
- Search filters the loaded product page in memory. The API contract exposes
  `limit` and `offset`, not a server-side query parameter, so the client asks
  for the first 50 products and filters locally.
- The products slice is a reference example. Replace it with the project's
  domain, or delete the package, the target dependency and the tab together.
{% endif %}

